# Warnings do not stop `run`: they print first, then the table.
mode: run
---- query
from '../../data/orders.csv' | where 1 == 1 | sort by orderId | take 2 | project orderId, amount
---- expected
warning[DS2102]: `where` condition is always true
  --> query:1:38
  |
1 | from '../../data/orders.csv' | where 1 == 1 | sort by orderId | take 2 | project orderId, amount
  |                                      ^^^^^^ true for every row, so `where` keeps them all
  |
  = help: if this is on purpose, remove the `where`: it has no effect

warning[DS2103]: `sort` key without `asc` or `desc`
  --> query:1:55
  |
1 | from '../../data/orders.csv' | where 1 == 1 | sort by orderId | take 2 | project orderId, amount
  |                                                       ^^^^^^^ sorted ascending, while KQL sorts descending by default
  |
  = help: write the direction: `orderId asc`, or `orderId desc` for largest first

orderId | amount
string  | real
--------+-------
o-0001  |  183.5
o-0002  |   88.5
